==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|chastize}} (archaic in British English and rare in American English)

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂eǵ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|chastisen}}, from {{der|en|fro|chastier}}, from {{der|en|la|castīgō}}. See also the doublets {{doublet|en|chasten|castigate|notext=1}} and cf. also {{l|en|chaste}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/tʃæˈstaɪz/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-chastise.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈt͡ʃæstaɪz/|/t͡ʃæˈstaɪz/}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪz|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[punish]] (someone), especially by [[corporal punishment]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1809|author=Flavius Josephus|title=The first eleven books of the Antiquities of the Jews, with a table of the Jewish coins, weights and measures|page=402
|passage=and if his father had '''chastised''' them with whips, they must expect that he would do it with scorpions.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=Nyx Smith|title=Shadowrun Legends: Striper Assassin|publisher=Catalyst Game Labs
|passage=“There is a man who must be '''chastised''',” she says softly, lightly. “'''Chastised''' in a physical way. It should not be difficult. Not for you.”}}
# To [[castigate]]; to [[severely]] [[scold]] or [[censure]] (someone).
# To lightly [[criticize]] or [[correct]] (someone).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=Eric Porter|title=What Is This Thing Called Jazz?: African American Musicians as Artists, Critics, and Activists|publisher=Univ of California Press|isbn=9780520232969|page=50
|passage=While Ellington voiced praise and respect for Benny Goodman and some white bandleaders, he gently '''chastised''' others for profiting from “musical-simplification to the &#39;nth&#39; degree” and “reach[ing] a pleasing musical middle.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Patricia Colton|title=The Window Blind|publisher=AuthorHouse|isbn=9781463460037|page=496
|passage=“You&#39;re not insensitive,” she lightly '''chastised'''. “I love you.” “Love you too.”}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2017|author=Ava Stone|title=A Scandalous Ruse
|passage=“Greg,” she lightly '''chastised'''. “You&#39;re not supposed to move your lips.” “Yes, I know. I&#39;m a horrible subject. But do answer the question, Bella.”}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2019|author=Eliza Ellis|title=Hers to Kiss|publisher=Eliza Ellis
|passage=“You could&#39;ve trusted me,” Pete gently '''chastised'''. “I can handle it.” He sat on the edge of her bed. “I was afraid to, honey. I know how stressed you&#39;ve been with the camp {{...}}”}}

